roves piece activity without creating weaknesses.  \n\n**Reason:**  \nCentralizing the rook on an open file supports future central pawn breaks and coordinates pieces. Other pawn moves are less urgent or create weaknesses; moving a rook from a1 doesn’t yet have a clear purpose.  \n\n**Answer:** R: f1-e1'}
