ack tactics involving the knight.\n\nReason: The move **P: f2-f4** is the most aggressive and forcing. It attacks Black's queen, which is currently in an active position, forcing it to retreat or move. This gains a tempo and helps White establish a stronger pawn center, potentially preparing for kingside expansion. It also opens up possibilities for the rook on e1 to support further advances. It’s a proactive move that seizes the initiative.\n\nAnswer: P: f2-f4"}
